From eaed6fd153c0511c33eca6134cae45745bd8b7f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:44:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 147/156] toolkit: link only the Qt modules Gecko uses (Core,
 Gui)

Network, Positioning, PrintSupport, Quick and Widgets were checked for and
linked into libxul, but nothing in Gecko or EmbedLite includes them, and
MOZ_ENABLE_QTNETWORK is set but never tested. On a phone with 1 GB of RAM
every library loaded at startup counts; the embedder links its own Qt
modules.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 toolkit/moz.configure | 12 +++++-------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/toolkit/moz.configure b/toolkit/moz.configure
index a8a231f0245b..7c511a6394d4 100644
--- a/toolkit/moz.configure
+++ b/toolkit/moz.configure
@@ -597,20 +597,18 @@ def toolkit_qt(toolkit):
 with only_when(toolkit_qt):
     set_config("MOZ_ENABLE_QT", True)
     set_define("MOZ_ENABLE_QT", True)
-    set_config("MOZ_ENABLE_QTNETWORK", True)
-    set_define("MOZ_ENABLE_QTNETWORK", True)
     set_define("QT_NO_KEYWORDS", True)
 
+    # Only the Qt modules Gecko's code uses: Core (QString, QUrl, QTimer,
+    # QThread, QObject, the event dispatcher) and Gui (QGuiApplication,
+    # QDesktopServices). Network, Positioning, PrintSupport, Quick and
+    # Widgets were linked into libxul without a user, and each is one more
+    # library to load. The embedder (qtmozembed) links what it needs itself.
     qt_base = pkg_check_modules(
         "MOZ_QT_BASE",
         [
             "Qt5Core",
             "Qt5Gui",
-            "Qt5Network",
-            "Qt5Positioning",
-            "Qt5PrintSupport",
-            "Qt5Quick",
-            "Qt5Widgets",
             "gio-unix-2.0",
             "glib-2.0",
             "gobject-2.0",
